  "design": [
    "Native command discovery owns ExternalScriptInfo, file decoding and defining-language policy. The runtime hashes the same decoded text it reparses, preserving the defining path.",
    "Expected SHA256 is lowercase hexadecimal over decoded source text encoded as UTF8, excluding the file BOM.",
    "Fresh native compilation data avoids modifying cached script clones. The shared lazy clause installer compiles optimized/unoptimized callbacks without initializing parameter attributes early.",
    "Ordinary call-operator invocation owns authorization and binding exactly once. The runtime does not set SignatureChecked or call authorization manually.",
    "The generated-root test replaces the handwritten prototype. The remaining fixture only records callback count; production runtime supplies native invocation preparation."
  ],
  "observableProof": [
    "Allowed original/generated invocation performs one authorization, one parameter attribute construction, one default evaluation and one generated callback.",
    "Denied invocation performs one authorization and zero parameter attribute constructions, defaults or callbacks. Source mismatch and restricted invocation fail before these effects.",
    "Both Windows hosts preserve four generated-root binding/storage/context cases and terminating validation rejection. Existing basic native-function behavior passes as a sibling."
  ],
  "earlierFailures": [
    "The first run failed 2/4: unavailable Get-FileHash in the isolated Windows PowerShell test state, and duplicate authorization caused by explicit ValidateScriptInfo before ordinary dispatch.",
    "The probe hashes through System.Security.Cryptography, and ordinary invocation now owns authorization. The corrected run passed 4/4; the final source after prototype removal passed 11/11."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The helper and native root lowering remain internal to compiler delivery; executable explain/build and packaged launcher do not select this route.",
    "Synthetic original/generated host qualification only; no new unchanged application, admitted root or complete-function gain.",
    "Claimed runtime hosts: Windows PowerShell 5.1/net472 and PowerShell 7/net10.0, FullLanguage. WDAC, signed execution policy and broader system/file policy are not live-qualified.",
    "Artifact source/dependency locks, declaration registration/order, launcher admission, full caller metadata and consequential stream/stop/cleanup qualification remain open.",
    "Counts unchanged: 544/565 emitted, 21 retained, fifteen justified hosted and six unqualified WPF functions.",
    "No aggregate gate/census, PR, merge or release."
  ]
